      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1356404062,
      "text": "Stylosanthes humilis, the Townsville stylo, is a species of flowering plant in the family Fabaceae, native to the New World Tropics, and widely introduced as a forage to the tropics of Africa, India, Southeast Asia, Malesia, and Australia. A nutritionally valuable forage plant, it was nearly wiped out in Australia in the 1970s by an outbreak of the fungus Colletotrichum gloeosporioides, which causes anthracnose disease."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Stylosanthes humilis",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stylosanthes_humilis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 160822361,
      "text": "Stylosanthes humilis es una especie de planta floral del género Stylosanthes, categorizada en la tribu Dalbergieae, de la subfamilia Faboideae."
    }
  },
